        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: दिग्भ्रमः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दिग्भ्रमः — digbhramaḥ — \"losing one's bearings\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वने पथिकस्य दिग्भ्रमः भवति। vane pathikasya digbhramaḥ bhavati. In the forest the wayfarer loses his bearings."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दिग्भ्रमः (digbhramaḥ) is built from diś, \"a direction\", and bhrama, \"wandering, confusion\", from the root √bhram, \"to wander\"; MW gives the compound as confusion about the quarters of the compass, mistaking the way (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
