              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भ्रान्तः — bhrāntaḥ — \"astray; wandering\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भ्रान्तः पथिकः ग्रामं न प्राप्नोति। bhrāntaḥ pathikaḥ grāmaṃ na prāpnoti. The wayfarer who has gone astray does not reach the village."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भ्रान्तः (bhrāntaḥ) comes from the root √bhram, \"to wander\", which also gives bhramati, \"wanders\": it is the participle, \"having wandered\", and MW gives bhrānta as roaming about and as confused (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
